course: dictionary
lesson: 14993
title: Reproductive: making new and making copies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reproductive is an adjective, a describing word. It has two meanings. The first is to do with having young or making new living things. The second is to do with copying something, such as a picture. Context tells you which one is meant.
explain: In science, «The reproductive system is the set of body parts that let an animal have young.» Here reproductive is about living things making babies. Phrases to notice are «reproductive system», «reproductive organs» and «reproductive cycle».
explain: In art and printing, «The shop sold reproductive copies of the famous painting.» The copies are not the first painting. They are made to look the same, so reproductive means to do with copying. A good check is to swap in a simpler word, such as copying, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Reproductive is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as system, organs or copies.
fact: «Reproductive» means to do with having young or making new living things.
fact: In a flower, «reproductive parts» include the stamen and the carpel.
fact: «Reproductive» can also mean to do with copying something, such as a picture.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning: look at the words around the word, such as «system», «copies» or «flower».
exercise: «The reproductive system of a rabbit helps it to have babies.» What does reproductive mean here? | *To do with having young | To do with moving quickly | Lasting a very long time | To do with eating food
exercise: «The shop sold reproductive copies of the famous painting.» What does reproductive mean here? | *To do with copying a picture | To do with growing trees | To do with cooking dinner | To do with swimming fast
exercise: Which of these is a reproductive part of a flower? | *Stamen | Root | Petal | Leaf
test: Which phrase in science means the body parts that let living things have young? | *Reproductive system | Reproductive copy | Reproductive picture | Reproductive cycle
test: Which sentence uses reproductive to mean copying? | *The museum printed reproductive versions of the old map | The reproductive system of a frog lays eggs | The reproductive organs help plants grow seeds | The reproductive cycle takes many months
exam: Which meaning is correct for reproductive in «the reproductive organs of a plant»? | Very old and worn out | *To do with having young or making new living things | Quick and noisy | To do with painting pictures
